   Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
   loopkit targets pi as its harness and pins pi-coding-agent on the 0.80.x line.

2) loop-engineering — MIT License
   Copyright (c) cobusgreyling
   https://github.com/cobusgreyling/loop-engineering
   loopkit borrows the "machine-readable work registry, validated in CI" pattern.
   loopkit forks out two footguns: a vendor-directory-grep detector (loopkit
   requires a re-runnable, repo-structure-aware detector command instead) and a
   dogfood that auto-merges at zero approvals (loopkit keeps a human checkpoint
   via its never-auto-merge invariant).

